## 7. Code Style & Standards
    General:
    -  TypeScript preferred for all files
    -  Modular, reusable code
    -  Meaningful variable and function names
    -  ESLint & Prettier configuration enforced

    Frontend (Next.js + Vite):
    -  File-based routing in pages/
    -  API routes in pages/api/
    -  Component-based architecture
    -  Use React Query or SWR for async data fetching
    -  TailwindCSS utility-first styling
    -  Accessibility: WCAG 2.1 compliance

    Backend:
    -  RESTful or GraphQL API endpoints
    -  Route naming: /api/v1/resource/:id
    -  Validation middleware for request payloads
    -  Error handling middleware

